  "notes": [
    "Tender's Safe called Comptroller _setPriceOracle, moving the oracle pointer from 0x4df9b2246bb592823fa60872e4f1a636f1be7473 to this GMXPriceOracle. No later NewPriceOracle event occurs before the exploit; the fix at block 67558205 reverted the pointer.",
    "Two campaigns merged. (1) 2023-03-07 07:13 UTC: liquidation bot 0x3ac52d0e (EOA 0x14c07a5f) liquidated two healthy GMX borrowers for 3 and 1 wei of GMX and redeemed 18.681895076176123477 ETH of their seized tETH; the protocol seize share that went to Tender reserves is excluded. (2) 08:24-08:44 UTC: attacker 0x896df375 supplied about 1 GMX and made 27 defect-enabled borrows, listed at their exact Borrow amounts. The first borrow, 0.01 ETH, was within legitimate capacity and is excluded. The attacker's collateral is not netted. The attacker later repaid the debt and kept 62.158670296 ETH as a bounty; that return does not reduce gross loss.",
    "The anchor is a liquidation by an apparently generic liquidation bot, not by the publicly reported attacker; it is the earliest successful transaction that benefits from the defective tGMX price."
  ]
